  "worked_solution": "First, we need to find the common ratio. We are told that ${a}_{1}=896$ and ${a}_{4}=112,$ so we can find the common ratio using a formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{n-m} & =\\frac{{a}_{n}}{{a}_{m}} \\\\ {r}^{4-1} & =\\frac{{a}_{4}}{{a}_{1}} \\\\ {r}^{4-1} & =\\frac{112}{896} \\\\ {r}^{3} & =\\frac{1}{8} \\\\ {r}^{3} & ={(\\frac{1}{2})}^{3} \\\\ r & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we know the common ratio is $r=\\frac{1}{2}$, we can use the same formula to solve for the value of $k$ such that ${a}_{k}=14:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{n-m} & =\\frac{{a}_{n}}{{a}_{m}} \\\\ {r}^{k-4} & =\\frac{{a}_{k}}{{a}_{4}} \\\\ {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{k-4} & =\\frac{14}{112} \\\\ {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{k-4} & =\\frac{1}{8} \\\\ {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{k-4} & ={(\\frac{1}{2})}^{3} \\\\ k-4 & =3 \\\\ k & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$",
